1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,408
Should everyone at a merchant see and do everything?

2
00:00:03,458 --> 00:00:11,544
In a shop, the owner, the accountant and the cashier each have their own badge, and each badge opens only the doors that job needs.

3
00:00:11,594 --> 00:00:13,872
A merchant's team works the same way.

4
00:00:13,922 --> 00:00:20,808
Each person has their own login and one of four roles: admin, accountant, operator, or observer.

5
00:00:20,858 --> 00:00:22,680
An admin invites people.

6
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:28,656
Each one sets their own password and an authenticator app on their phone, because these people can give money back.

7
00:00:28,706 --> 00:00:33,816
Every action names the roles that may run it, and nothing more: least privilege.

8
00:00:33,866 --> 00:00:37,608
Changing someone's role or blocking them takes effect at once.

9
00:00:37,658 --> 00:00:43,176
And a merchant can never lose its last admin, so nobody is ever locked out of their own shop.

10
00:00:43,226 --> 00:00:45,528
Next: the merchant's websites.
